1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,635
How does water in a reservoir

2
00:00:02,675 --> 00:00:04,466
become electricity for a city?

3
00:00:06,375 --> 00:00:09,595
In this example, a head of 400 metres

4
00:00:09,635 --> 00:00:12,529
and 8.5 cubic metres per second

5
00:00:12,569 --> 00:00:14,602
yield about 30 megawatts,

6
00:00:14,642 --> 00:00:17,283
after turbine and generator losses.

7
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,930
At the nozzle, the water pressure

8
00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:21,684
becomes a high-speed jet.

9
00:00:24,234 --> 00:00:25,927
The jet strikes the buckets

10
00:00:25,967 --> 00:00:28,146
of the Pelton turbine tangentially

11
00:00:28,186 --> 00:00:29,627
and changes direction.

12
00:00:30,826 --> 00:00:33,015
That interaction makes the runner turn.

13
00:00:33,849 --> 00:00:36,510
Its electromagnets
produce a magnetic field

14
00:00:36,550 --> 00:00:38,373
that moves past the windings

15
00:00:38,413 --> 00:00:41,065
of the stator, which stays fixed.

16
00:00:43,669 --> 00:00:45,614
That change induces voltage.

17
00:00:46,210 --> 00:00:47,762
Once the breaker closes,

18
00:00:47,802 --> 00:00:48,980
it can deliver power.

19
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,722
The stator stays still,

20
00:00:51,762 --> 00:00:53,756
but the currents in its three phases

21
00:00:53,796 --> 00:00:54,778
change over time.

22
00:00:55,518 --> 00:00:58,857
Each phase produces a
magnetic contribution

23
00:00:58,897 --> 00:01:01,457
that pulses along a fixed axis.

24
00:01:02,297 --> 00:01:05,287
Added together, they form
a field that rotates

25
00:01:05,327 --> 00:01:06,878
with constant amplitude.

26
00:01:08,418 --> 00:01:11,397
Under load, this field
interacts with the rotor.

27
00:01:13,037 --> 00:01:15,244
The transformer steps the voltage up

28
00:01:15,284 --> 00:01:18,965
from 13.8 to 230 kilovolts.

29
00:01:19,495 --> 00:01:22,741
Understanding the plant means
following that whole chain,

30
00:01:22,781 --> 00:01:24,004
from the water resource

31
00:01:24,044 --> 00:01:25,457
to the needs of the user.
